/E (A retail store maintains a product catalog containing specifications for all items sold, each with a description, price, and unique ID. The physical store at a specific location houses multiple point-of-sale registers. When a customer makes a purchase, a cashier initiates a new sale on a register, creating a sale record with date and time information. For each item purchased, the system creates a sales line item noting the quantity sold, which is linked to the corresponding product specification from the catalog. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [1 2]
